# Copy to ~/.config/fumox/fumox.env and adjust. The quadlet units read this
# file via EnvironmentFile= (see podman-systemd.unit(5)); after editing it,
# run `systemctl --user daemon-reload` and restart the units:
#
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user restart fumox-server.service fumox-probe.service fumox-meow.service
#   # ...or the pod units the README brings up:
#   # systemctl --user restart fumox-pod.service fumox-worker-pod.service
#
# The values are parsed by systemd's EnvironmentFile=, not by a shell:
# $VAR references are not expanded, values containing spaces or quotes
# must be wrapped in quotes, and a `#` comment only works on its own
# line — a trailing comment would become part of the value.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/fumox
#   install -m 600 docker/quadlet/fumox.env.example ~/.config/fumox/fumox.env
#
# The file holds a secret (the controller token below), so it must not be
# readable by other users: mode 600, owner = you. `install -m 600` sets it
# at creation, so the file is never briefly world-readable.
#
# These are the SHARED variables: the server, the probe and the kernel read
# them. The admin panel variables (the login token above all) live in
# fumox-admin.env, which only the server reads.

# Controller secret for the meow-rs external-controller REST API. The
# kernel refuses to start without one (an unauthenticated controller can
# rewrite the proxy configuration) and the probe presents it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Generate a random value:
#
#   printf 'FUMOX_MEOW__API_TOKEN=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
#
# and paste the result below. Any character outside [A-Za-z0-9._-] is
# refused by the kernel's entrypoint.
FUMOX_MEOW__API_TOKEN=

# Optional: TOML config file inside the container. Unset (default) makes the
# binaries read /app/config/app.toml from the mounted config volume, the
# image default. Point it at a differently named file in that volume when
# needed; the file must exist, a missing one fails the startup loudly.
# That volume is the host's %h/fumox/config mounted at /app/config (see
# fumox-server.container): put your app.toml into ~/fumox/config.
#FUMOX_CONFIG=/app/config/app.toml

# Optional: T2 delay-test URL. Override if the default is blocked in your
# region (default: https://www.gstatic.com/generate_204).
#FUMOX_MEOW__TEST_URL=https://www.gstatic.com/generate_204

# Optional: let the probe dial loopback/RFC1918/link-local/CGNAT targets
# harvested from feeds (disables the probe-side SSRF guard). Local testing
# only, feeds are untrusted input. Default: false.
#FUMOX_PROBE__ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true
